<title>USA: Alter trigger, adopt US sugar quota plan - Industry.</title>
<headline>Alter trigger, adopt US sugar quota plan - Industry.</headline>
<byline>Charles Abbott</byline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The sugar industry generally welcomed a proposed formula for setting the U.S. import quota but, in comments submitted to the Agriculture Department, disagreed over the trigger level for letting in more sugar.</p>
<p>Of 18 comments received by midday Friday, only four opposed the USDA plan. Friday was the deadline to comment. USDA intends to rule on the fiscal 1997 quota by September 13.</p>
<p>It has proposed a tariff-rate quota of 2.475 million tonnes. Of that, 1.875 million would be allocated at once with potential adjustments in November, February and May.</p>
</text>
